  "properties": {
    "title": "Field data collection using Input app, QGIS and Mergin",
    "description": "Using open source software, users will be able to collect data from their mobile devices collaboratively with other participants and bring the data back in QGIS.\n\nInput app is a free and open source app for Android and iOS based on QGIS which allows users to take their QGIS project/data in the field and then capture/edit data. The data then seamlessly synchronised to their desktop using the Mergin service.\r\n\r\nWith Mergin service, users can also see the history of changes to the data and share their projects with other users to collaborate.",
